# Fixed 2026-11-24, defect 2756, lane-panel258-r1 (panel 258's R1,
# provisional, author ratification pending; the sitting's `lendjump`): a
# callback lends a buffer to C, `@md: [u8] counted_by 4096 lent`, and C
# `longjmp`s out of the call it was lent to, 20,000 times. A correct program.
# Symptom: exit 0 holding 334,741,504 bytes resident against 2,998,272 where
# C returns: each jump left its region mapped and the next lend mapped one a
# depth higher, outside every gate.
# Cause: a region is given back by the lending function after the call,
# which the jump skipped, and nothing else ever gave it back.
# Fix: each region remembers the lending function's frame
# (`runtime/parts/lend.c`, `runtime/parts/callback.c`), and a lend, a thunk's
# entry or a give below the newest region first gives back the regions of
# frames below its own. The resident size is not this case's to judge; its
# output and its end are, and the shapes beside it below.
extern "fixedbugs-2752-levels.h"
    function lv_try(cb: (function(i64) -> i64), n: i64) -> i64
    function lv_fill_throw(@md: [u8] counted_by 4096 lent) -> i32

function body(n: i64) -> i64
    md: [u8] @= []
    print_nothing(n: lv_fill_throw(@md))
    return md.len() + n

function print_nothing(n: i32)
    if n == 99
        print("never")

function main()
    total: i64 @= 0

    for _ in range(from: 0, to: 20000)
        total @ total + lv_try(cb: body, n: 1)

    print("jumped, sum ", total)

# Corrected 2026-11-25, lane land259 (panel 259's R1, route E,
# provisional, author ratification pending): the fix above is gone. No take
# and no lend is judged given back by its frame's address any more, since an
# order of addresses a switch of stacks C makes can falsify handed live
# values to other frames (panel 259's cells); what the frames C left held
# stays held until the program ends, counted against the room's 1 GiB with
# every lent region's mapped bytes (spec section 13), and this program's
# jumps stay under it, so its output and end are as they were.
